&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Applications are now open for our January cohort - &lt;a href=&quot;https://bit.ly/afpsafety&quot;&gt;apply here by October 30.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anthropic Fellows Program overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Anthropic Fellows Program is designed to foster AI research and engineering talent. We provide funding and mentorship to promising technical talent - regardless of previous experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fellows will primarily use external infrastructure (e.g. open-source models, public APIs) to work on an empirical project aligned with our research priorities, with the goal of producing a &lt;strong&gt;public output&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g. a paper submission). In one of our earlier cohorts, over 80% of fellows produced papers.&amp;nbsp;We run multiple cohorts of Fellows each year and review applications on a rolling basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to expect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 months of full-time research&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct mentorship from Anthropic researchers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a shared workspace (in either Berkeley, California or London, UK)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connection to the broader AI safety and security research community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weekly stipend of 3,850 USD / 2,310 GBP / 4,300 CAD + benefits (these vary by country)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Funding for compute (~$15k/month) and other research expenses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview process&

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is growing quickly across Asia Pacific, and our International Recruiting Coordination team is building for it. As our first Recruiting Coordinator based in Singapore, you&#39;ll deliver a warm, high touch interview experience for candidates across APAC, including Japan, Korea, India, Australia, New Zealand and South East Asia. You&#39;ll partner closely with our APAC recruiters and recruiting managers, be the local point of contact for candidates and interviewers in the region and help keep hiring moving around the clock as part of a follow the sun coordination model with your teammates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As you&#39;ll be first in seat, you&#39;ll also help shape how coordination works in a region where we&#39;re still building: spotting what&#39;s missing, documenting what works and making it easier for the people who join after you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own coordination for your region end to end and act as our go to operator for APAC hiring logistics, working independently with support from your manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule a high volume of APAC interview loops, from hiring manager screens through onsites, debriefs and reference calls, across multiple time zones, languages and stakeholder calendars.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the primary point of contact for candidates on logistics, with a warm, clear and culturally aware ton

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Recruiting Research Scientist to join our People Data Solutions team. You’ll be the research expert supporting our Recruiting organization, using rigorous scientific methods to advance our understanding of recruiting funnels, interview effectiveness, candidate experience, and recruiting capacity. This role sits at the intersection of organizational science, behavioral research, and people strategy – developing novel frameworks and conducting systematic research that drives evidence-based people decisions across our growing organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role offers the opportunity to make a significant impact on both our recruiting practices and the broader field of people science at a leading AI safety company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research design &amp;amp; scientific inquiry&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design and execute systematic research studies to answer fundamental questions about recruiting funnel health, assessment quality, candidate experience, and quality of hire&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Generate and test hypotheses about sourcing strategies, interview design, and selection decisions using rigorous experimental and quasi-experimental methods&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conduct mixed-method research to understand what are the drivers and blockers to recruiting operations.&

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s Safeguards Enforcement team detects and mitigates misuse of Claude, and much of that work depends on people: a growing human review workforce made up of full-time staff, contractors, vendors and BPO partners. As that workforce scales across a widening range of harm areas, the programs that bring people in, give them the right access, and roll them off cleanly have to keep pace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Program Manager for Safeguards Workforce Operations, you’ll own those programs end to end. You’ll run onboarding, offboarding, device provisioning and access provisioning for every worker type we use, working hands-on with the requests themselves while you build the processes that make them repeatable. You’ll partner with Enforcement leads to turn shifting priorities into capacity plans, and carry those plans through with our vendor partners. Because this role supports every Safeguards Enforcement program, you’ll also connect the dots across Anthropic, working with IT, People Operations, Security, Contingent Workforce, Human Data Operations and other teams running scaled human review to streamline practices and keep standards consistent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who likes fixing broken things at speed. The landscape moves quickly, priorities change often, and the work is an even mix of direct execution and program building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;

